Summary of behavioural changes to existing code:

  * Float32 prior distributions are widened to float64 rather than rejected.
  * A warning is emitted when media history is too short for the adstock
    window, which otherwise zero-pads silently.
  * Non-finite variables are excluded from the VIF check rather than aborting
    it.
  * Several input-validation errors now name the offending column, coordinate
    or value.
  * Test-only fixes for protobuf >= 6 and for Python 3.11 mock behaviour.
  * The generated HTML report shows credible intervals on the response-curve
    chart, which previously passed `include_ci=False`, and carries a caveat
    stating that those intervals are conditional on the assumed saturation
    shape.
  * Multi-channel charts use an explicit colour-blind-safe categorical range
    instead of falling back to Vega-Lite's default scheme.
  * The budget-allocation chart is a labelled bar rather than a pie whose
    values were reachable only on hover.
  * The report loads pinned Vega library versions instead of unversioned URLs,
    so an archived report keeps rendering as it did when it was written.

This fork's distribution is named `meridian-mmm-fork`, not `google-meridian`.
The import path is unchanged (`import meridian`), but the published package is
deliberately distinct so it cannot be mistaken for Google's release.

No change alters the model's statistical specification. Feature requests that
would have done so are declined in TRIAGE.md with reasons.
